# Version5 restore point

When the user says **Restore Version5** (or similar):

1. Discard or set aside later edits and restore the tree to git tag `Version5` (commit on `master` / `Version5-branch`).
2. Prefer non-destructive first: `git switch master` then `git reset --hard Version5` only after confirming there is no uncommitted work the user wants kept (or stash/commit it first).
3. Do not continue applying post-Version5 feature work from chat history after a restore unless the user asks.

Restore markers created 2026-10-07:

- Annotated tag: `Version5`
- Branch: `Version5-branch`
- Initial commit message: `Initial commit: BZ Music Version5 snapshot.`
